            {
                "entry_id": "d8ed0826-c417-38fa-b97c-766bae3d1da2",
                "word": "pash",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "922f6915-669e-489a-a814-0dab53de2e62",
                        "entry_id": "d8ed0826-c417-38fa-b97c-766bae3d1da2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pashes"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "f9eaf537-eba9-3060-a1b7-632c7146c19c",
                        "entry_id": "d8ed0826-c417-38fa-b97c-766bae3d1da2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A smash, a crash; a heavy collision, fall, or blow, or the sound made by it."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "55ced02b-bb55-424f-85af-8c44b88f3733",
                                "sense_id": "f9eaf537-eba9-3060-a1b7-632c7146c19c",
                                "text": "[…] the pash of a crushed skull, an oath, or a grunt caused by the impact of a rifle's muzzle against the abdomen transfixed by its bayonet."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "73c34536-5cb7-4cbf-b4c2-7cc62fcbfe15",
                                "sense_id": "f9eaf537-eba9-3060-a1b7-632c7146c19c",
                                "text": "[Neither] the pash of a hoof on the marge, crack of whip, nor the shout of driver gladdens the quiet: the foul weeds knot, strangling the sluggish flow of the waterway; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1699dece-562e-3607-94af-b9adf9f2afaa",
                        "entry_id": "d8ed0826-c417-38fa-b97c-766bae3d1da2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A sudden and heavy fall or gush of rain, snow, hail or other water."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dialectal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "20c32c0d-344f-45cf-865f-2ecaad5f8466",
                                "sense_id": "1699dece-562e-3607-94af-b9adf9f2afaa",
                                "text": "BACKEN, To retard, \"This pash o'rain 'ul backen our potatoes.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7bb8dc6-a205-4a95-b467-5e322d4458de",
                                "sense_id": "1699dece-562e-3607-94af-b9adf9f2afaa",
                                "text": "A pash of rain then raised it about 6 inches, but four dry days reduced it to its previous level."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c08a929b-b00e-43ef-b267-100c0b715449",
                                "sense_id": "1699dece-562e-3607-94af-b9adf9f2afaa",
                                "text": "Mony a thunner pash it's been oot in."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5ac869af-52f7-4979-96d2-5a3d941b47c5",
                                "sense_id": "1699dece-562e-3607-94af-b9adf9f2afaa",
                                "text": "... the water came down with such a pash that ..."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "347add45-fb37-4bcc-8155-66aec30e52c9",
                                "sense_id": "1699dece-562e-3607-94af-b9adf9f2afaa",
                                "text": "Labes, a great fall, or pash of rain or hail, etc."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
                "entry_id": "6aed93ca-abf7-3364-85ca-76e30751bb29",
